    - To run project : npm run start OR npm start
    - To buld your project in production: npm run build

    => JSX : 
        - It is not HTML in javascript. It is HTML-like or XML-like syntax.
        - It is combination of HTML and Javascript.
        - JSX (transpiled before it reaches the JS) - Parcel - Babel
        - JSX => Babel transpiles it to React.createElement => ReactElement => Javascript engine Object => HTMLElement(render)
        - If you are giving an attribute in jsx (className, tabIndex) should be in camelCase.
    => Babel : 
        - Babel is a javascript compiler. It takes JSX and convert into the code that browser (JS engine) understand.
        - It converts the JSX element into react element.

    Extension install : 
        - Prettier Code
        - Bracket Pair Colorization
        - ESLint
        - Better Comments

    - React Element :
        - lower case letter or camelCase
    - React Component
        - Two types of React component
            1. Class Based component - Old version of writing code
            2. Functional component - New version of writing code => It is just a normal javscript function.
                - A function which returns jsx or react element that is called Functional component.
                Note : When you are creating any component, Name should be in Uppercase.Function component which return some jsx.
                - Example :
                    const HeadingFunComponent = () =>{
                        return <h1>It is React Functional Component</h1>
                    }

    - We can put react element inside React Functional component and vice versa.
    - To render react element => root.render(reactElement)
    - To render react functional component => root.render(<ReactComponent />)

